// coop_puppet.cpp -- the peer's body: summon/adopt, shell mesh, animation,
// drive/travel/patrol, World Partition streaming sources and the stream verdict.
//
// Ported from G:\Freespace\shell_coop\ms2-coop\mod\CoopMod\Scripts\main.lua:
//   188-491   body + animation block (ANIMBONES, ANIM_MESH, PUPPET_MESH, LOCO,
//             SEQ_PATHS, SEQ, ANIM, GSTATICS/WORLD/rt, skinnedMeshesOf,
//             missingAssets, GAMELOAD/requestGameLoad, findObjectByPath/findAsset,
//             footBonesOnMesh, BODY_STATE, APPLIED_BODY, PUPPET_HIDDEN,
//             BODY_ATTEMPTS, puppetMeshComponent, applyBodyMesh,
//             ensurePuppetBody, syncBodyChoice, animOff, PEER_MONTAGE, normDeg,
//             playSeq, setRate, playMontage, updatePuppetAnimation)
//   492-606   S/enter/pt, STREAM, streamSources, streamSetup, setupPuppet, bootTick
//   1607-1765 peerSpeed, drive counters, clearInput, teleportPuppet, PUPPET_SPEED,
//             prevPuppetPos, lastDriveT, peerEverSeen, setPuppetHidden, PUPPET_YAW,
//             travelTick, driveTick, PATROL, cmdPatrol, patrolTick
//   3738-3811 actorsNear, streamTick
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CRASH NOTES -- these are not opinions, each cost a run (docs/HANDOFF.md 5,
// docs/NATIVE-PORT.md 4). Do not "fix" any of them:
//
//  * The puppet is POSITIONED DIRECTLY (K2_SetActorLocation / K2_SetActorRotation).
//    NEVER SetMovementMode(1) + AddMovementInput: a possession-less pawn in
//    Walking mode crashes inside the movement tick, 3/3 (HANDOFF.md 5.6).
//    kLegacyTeleportDist / kLegacyStopDist / kLegacyMaxSpeed / kLegacyMinSpeed /
//    kLegacyStuckTicks (coop_state.h, Lua 70-74) are the leftovers of that
//    abandoned drive: they are declared and never read. THERE IS NO STUCK
//    DETECTION -- the body snaps only when the distance is > 400 uu. Implementing
//    "the tuning constants" re-creates the crash. (SetMovementMode(1) in
//    Setup() is the Lua's own once-per-adopt call and does not feed input; the
//    crash needs the input vector.)
//  * SetAnimInstanceClass(nullptr) BEFORE SetSkeletalMeshAsset(shell), always:
//    swapping the mesh while a live AnimBP instance exists crashes in memcpy
//    during the anim re-init (HANDOFF.md 5.5).
//  * Animation is SetAnimationMode(1,true) ONCE, then SetAnimation / Play /
//    SetPlayRate. PlayAnimation() alone hung a client twice.
//  * RootMotionMode = 1 set ONCE right after that mode switch, otherwise a
//    root-motion clip drags the mesh off the capsule.
//  * The body stays hidden until there is a packet, the peer is live, the packet
//    is <= 3 s old AND the body is ready. A mesh swap re-applies PUPPET_HIDDEN;
//    it never un-hides.
//  * Every cached pointer goes through ue::IsValid before use; Reset() drops all
//    of them on a world change (docs/NATIVE-PORT.md 4.41 / HANDOFF.md 18: a guest
//    client died in ProcessEvent on a freed actor).
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CONTRACT-REQUEST (things coop_state.h / ms2_ue.h do not give this module)
//
//  1. ue::ConsoleCommand() is not in native\src\ms2_ue.h. The summon goes through
//     net::Console() (coop_state.h 8, "the ONLY way to spawn the puppet"), which
//     must also emit the Lua's "console [%s]" line (main.lua:181). Nothing here
//     logs a second one.
//  2. ue::GetWorld/GetPawn/GetPlayerController are not in ms2_ue.h either; this
//     module uses net::World()/net::Pawn() from coop_state.h.
//  3. ue::ToString(FName) / ue::MakeFName() are listed in the brief but absent
//     from ms2_ue.h. Bone names are resolved through
//     UKismetStringLibrary.Conv_NameToString instead (FNameToStr below), which
//     needs no new ue:: primitive. If ue::ToString lands, FNameToStr can go.
//  4. ue::GetCDO() is absent; the KismetStringLibrary CDO is resolved by path
//     ("/Script/Engine.Default__KismetStringLibrary").
//  5. No native LoadAsset. requestGameLoad() keeps the whole Lua gate (LOAD_ON.txt
//     default off, 3 tries, 2 s gap, one job at a time) but the queued job can
//     only re-query the object array (ue::FindObject); it cannot force a load.
//     LOAD_ON stays off by default exactly as in Lua (main.lua:253-277).
//  6. FOLDED IN: StartTravel / StartTp / MovementMode / OwnStreamingIncomplete are
//     now declared in coop_state.h section 10 (they used to live in a private
//     coop_puppet_extra.h). The definitions at the bottom of this file are
//     unchanged; coop_net calls StartTp/StartTravel instead of writing PuppetState
//     itself, so the "owner writes" rule holds.
//  7. PEER_MONTAGE has no `at` field in MontageSig. In Lua PEER_MONTAGE.at is
//     always == lastPeer.at (it is captured from the same `at` and only on a
//     fresh packet, and lastPeer.at does not advance otherwise), so the montage
//     play head reads state().peer.at. No new field is needed -- but that
//     equality must hold in net::ApplyPeer.
// ===========================================================================

